    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0300" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg276"/>

                <head>Mr. True to Mr.
                        Harvey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Madeira</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 19, 1863</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have just received, per steamer Sampson,
                    a letter from our consul at Teneriffe, saying that the confederate steamer
                    Georgia, Captain Maury, had arrived there on the 15th instant from the Cape,
                    having on board the captain and crew of the ship Bold Hunter, of Boston, burned
                    by her at sea.</p>
                <p>As he writes that she is taking on 300 tons of coal, and was to leave on the
                    night of the 16th, and as this steamer seems to have changed her route for
                    Lisbon, I deem it proper to advise you of these facts.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, in great haste, yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE TRUE, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. E. Harvey</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >United States Minister, Lisbon.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
